ask_business: description, inputSchema  -The business answers your person by email, at +It carries their name and +email -(consent), +(consent): ask them first. The business answers by email,  parameters: +name and -Where the business can answer. Only an +Who the request is from, as your person agreed to give it to this business: their name and their -address and a name: never +address. Never -answer. +answer: one that receives mail, never a no-reply one or one at .invalid, .test or localhost. -The name your person wants the business to use. +Your person's name, as they gave it for the business to use: with a letter in it and no @, and never a placeholder (N/A, Test, {{name}}). A business's inbox refuses a request without it, or with one that is not a name.
request_booking: description, inputSchema  -person. +person, with their name and the email address they agreed to give (consent): ask them first. -email, at the address your person agreed to give. +email.  parameters: +name and email address for its answer. input.contact input.contact description: Needed with start: who the request is from, as your person agreed to give it to this business: their name and their -input.contact input.contact description: Needed with start: where the business can answer. +Never a phone number. -answer. +answer: one that receives mail, never a no-reply one or one at .invalid, .test or localhost. -The name your person wants the business to use. +Your person's name, as they gave it for the business to use: with a letter in it and no @, and never a placeholder (N/A, Test, {{name}}
request_quote: description, inputSchema  +It carries their name and the email address they agreed to give (consent): ask them first. -email, at the address your person agreed to give (consent). +email.  parameters: +name and -Where the business can answer. Only an +Who the request is from, as your person agreed to give it to this business: their name and their -address and a name: never +address. Never -answer. +answer: one that receives mail, never a no-reply one or one at .invalid, .test or localhost. -The name your person wants the business to use. +Your person's name, as they gave it for the business to use: with a letter in it and no @, and never a placeholder (N/A, Test, {{name}}). A business's inbox refuses a request without it, or with one that is not a name.

list_channels: description  +Add a Slack channel or a webhook with create_channel;
added create_channel
added list_slack_channels

check_availability: description  -BILLING_ENTITLEMENTS_ENABLED=true -STRIPE_MODE=test/live +billing switched on (test or live)
discover_local: description  -matchedOn +matchedOn, hours, services -BILLING_ENTITLEMENTS_ENABLED=true -STRIPE_MODE=test/live; +billing switched on (test or live);
find_nearby_businesses: description  +hours with hoursSource, +services, -list. +list; an empty list adds suggested_categories to try.
get_business: description, inputSchema  -sign-in: +sign-in by id (business_id from find_business is also accepted). Returns +services,  parameters: +input.business_id
get_open_slots: description  -BILLING_ENTITLEMENTS_ENABLED=true -STRIPE_MODE=test/live; +billing switched on (test or live);
search_local_offerings: description  -BILLING_ENTITLEMENTS_ENABLED=true -STRIPE_MODE=test/live. +billing switched on (test or live).
